Look, that's New Year's Eve for ya.
瞧，这就是你的除夕夜。

00:57:40.380 --> 00:57:44.099
You're welcome for that turn of phrase.
不客气。

00:57:44.099 --> 00:57:50.780
Well, we like to end our episode with some viewer listener mail.
好吧，我们想用一些观众听众的邮件来结束我们的剧集。

00:57:50.780 --> 00:57:58.239
And we have a lovely letter today from Jessica and Craig is going to read it for us.
今天我们收到了杰西卡写的一封可爱的信，克雷格将为我们朗读。

00:57:58.239 --> 00:57:59.480
Yes, this is lovely.
是的，这很可爱。

00:57:59.480 --> 00:58:04.480
And a little conversation talking point emerges at the end of it.
最后出现了一个小谈话要点。

00:58:04.480 --> 00:58:05.320
So here we go, ready?
那么我们开始吧，准备好了吗？

00:58:05.320 --> 00:58:06.320
This is Jessica.
这是杰西卡。

00:58:06.320 --> 00:58:07.960
She says, hi, Josh and Craig.
她说，嗨，乔什和克雷格。

00:58:07.960 --> 00:58:09.760
Jessica here from New Brunswick, Canada.
杰西卡来自加拿大新不伦瑞克省。

00:58:09.760 --> 00:58:10.880
Shout out to Canada.
向加拿大喊话。

00:58:10.880 --> 00:58:12.679
We love our Canadian fans.
我们爱我们的加拿大球迷。

00:58:12.679 --> 00:58:15.639
And we love our Canadian characters as a plural.
我们喜欢加拿大的复数字符。

00:58:15.639 --> 00:58:18.780
I think we had a few over the years, mainly Robin.
我想这些年来我们有过一些，主要是罗宾。

00:58:18.780 --> 00:58:25.380
My husband Tristan introduced me to him when we first started dating and it quickly became a cherished part of our lives.
当我们第一次开始约会时，我的丈夫特里斯坦向他介绍了我，这很快就成为我们生活中珍贵的一部分。

00:58:25.380 --> 00:58:29.900
The show holds such significance to us that it actually played a role in our wedding day.
这个节目对我们来说意义重大，它实际上在我们的婚礼上发挥了作用。

00:58:29.900 --> 00:58:39.539
From gifting my soon to be husband of Blue French Horn to open the morning of the wedding, to having Heaven by the Walkman play during our recessional, great song.
从向我即将成为蓝色法国号的丈夫的礼物，到婚礼早上的开幕式，再到在我们经济衰退期间让随身听播放《天堂》，美妙的歌曲。

00:58:39.539 --> 00:58:41.619
You have to wait till the end of the series, you get to it.
你必须等到这个系列结束，你才能看到它。

00:58:41.619 --> 00:58:48.079
And the unforgettable moment of our bosses surprising us with a cameo of Josh during their heartfelt speech.
我们的老板在真诚的演讲中客串了乔什，这一令人难忘的时刻让我们感到惊讶。

00:58:48.079 --> 00:59:02.639
I know cameos might seem like a small gesture of celebrities, but hearing Josh say, as Ted Mosby said, love is the best thing we do on our wedding day, was nothing short of legendary captured beautifully in the photos and video footage of our reactions.
我知道客串可能看起来像是名人的一个小举动，但听到乔什说，正如泰德·莫斯比所说，爱是我们在婚礼当天做的最好的事情，这简直就是传奇，在我们的反应的照片和视频片段中完美地捕捉到了这一点。

00:59:02.639 --> 00:59:05.960
Please send us those, by the way, Jessica.
顺便说一句，杰西卡，请把那些寄给我们。

00:59:05.960 --> 00:59:13.760
It warms my heart to see how both of you remain humbled and perhaps a touch astonished by the profound impact your creation has had on countless lives.
看到你们俩保持谦逊，或许还对你们的创作对无数生命产生的深远影响感到惊讶，这让我感到温暖。

00:59:13.760 --> 00:59:21.920
My question for both of you is this, is there a show or film series that evokes the same feelings in you that Hemium does for its fans?
我想问你们俩的问题是，是否有一个节目或电影系列能够唤起你们与 Hemium 对其粉丝同样的感受？

00:59:21.920 --> 00:59:24.840
You're going to anticipate this journey of dissecting every last episode.
你将会期待这段剖析最后每一集的旅程。

00:59:24.840 --> 00:59:33.059
Please know that you both, and Carter, have conjured something truly spectacular, a treasure that will continue to resonate for years to come.
请知道，你们和卡特已经创造了一些真正壮观的东西，一件将在未来几年继续引起共鸣的宝藏。

00:59:33.059 --> 00:59:34.059
Thank you, Jessica.
谢谢你，杰西卡。

00:59:34.059 --> 00:59:34.900
Well, thanks, Jessica.
嗯，谢谢，杰西卡。

00:59:34.900 --> 00:59:38.340
What a lovely, every part of that, being part of their wedding.
成为他们婚礼的一部分，这一切真是太可爱了。

00:59:38.340 --> 00:59:40.019
I love that you did that cameo.
我喜欢你客串。

00:59:40.019 --> 00:59:46.692
I don't know if you remember doing that specific one years ago or not, did you know what was going to be part of a wedding?
我不知道你是否记得一年前做过这样的事，你知道婚礼会包含什么吗？

00:59:46.692 --> 00:59:51.520
I don't, I'm, I mean, I mean, I had asked, I always make a joke about being underdressed.
我不，我是，我是说，我是说，我问过，我总是开玩笑说衣着暴露。

00:59:51.520 --> 00:59:52.659
That's kind of money.
那是一笔钱。

00:59:53.860 --> 00:59:58.756
But yeah, I mean, I sometimes they'll say, can you throw in a Ted Mosby quote, you love.
但是，是的，我的意思是，有时他们会说，你能引用泰德·莫斯比的名言吗，你喜欢。

00:59:58.756 --> 01:00:03.875
And for me, that's like the one, you know, from, for a wedding, I think that's the best one.
对我来说，这就像婚礼上的那种，我认为那是最好的。

01:00:03.875 --> 01:00:04.375
Yeah.
是的。

01:00:04.375 --> 01:00:06.322
Yeah, it's the whole series, right?
是的，这是整个系列，对吧？

01:00:06.322 --> 01:00:12.721
That's that if you had a distilled series down to one line, that could, that could be in the running to be the one.
也就是说，如果你有一个精简到一行的系列，那可能就是那个。

01:00:12.500 --> 01:00:16.019
And I think it's, you know, there's different kinds of love.
我认为，你知道，爱有不同类型。

01:00:16.019 --> 01:00:17.754
Like we have that one word, but like C.S.
就像我们有这个词一样，但就像 C.S.

01:00:17.754 --> 01:00:19.699
Lewis has a book called The Four Loves, right?
刘易斯有一本书叫《四种爱》，对吗？

01:00:19.699 --> 01:00:30.659
It's like Eros and Philos, and like there's different, but I think love more broadly speaking is kind of how I'm able to, because there's certainly friendship, love.
就像厄洛斯和斐洛斯一样，虽然有不同，但我认为更广泛地说，爱是我能够做到的，因为肯定有友谊和爱情。

01:00:30.659 --> 01:00:32.585
It's so much about friendship.
这非常关乎友谊。

01:00:32.585 --> 01:00:34.126
It's mostly that, right?
大部分都是这样，对吧？

01:00:34.126 --> 01:00:39.005
In the end, it's a lot of of dates but the friendships there the whole time.
最后，虽然有很多次约会，但友谊始终存在。

01:00:39.005 --> 01:00:46.260
Do you have pieces of art that live and take residence in your heart the way that him, him, has heard these fans?
你是否有一些艺术作品像他、他听到这些歌迷的声音一样，活在你的心中？

01:00:46.260 --> 01:00:59.431
I mean, for me, I feel like what Jessica's talking about and I think the feeling she's talking about can only be achieved through a franchise, a series, something that goes on a while that you can spend that much time with.
我的意思是，对我来说，我感觉杰西卡正在谈论的事情，并且我认为她正在谈论的感觉只能通过特许经营，连续剧，持续一段时间的东西才能实现，你可以花很多时间。

01:00:59.431 --> 01:01:03.980
Your favorite movie that's like an hour hour and a half long, two hours long.
你最喜欢的电影大概一个半小时，两个小时长。

01:01:03.980 --> 01:01:07.500
You can go back into that world over and over, but it's kind of always that one thing.
你可以一遍又一遍地回到那个世界，但它总是那么一件事。

01:01:07.500 --> 01:01:14.219
It's hard to replicate that, but what she's talking about, what a TV series can give you, it's such a gift to get nine seasons to do a show.
这很难复制，但她所说的，电视剧可以给你什么，能拍九季的电视剧真是一份礼物。

01:01:14.219 --> 01:01:24.860
So for me, what comes up for me when she says that, is like, Star Wars, the Star Wars franchise, just getting to, that stretching across my entire childhood into my adult life.
所以对我来说，当她这么说时，我想到的就像是《星球大战》，《星球大战》系列，刚刚开始，它贯穿了我的整个童年，一直延伸到我的成年生活。

01:01:24.860 --> 01:01:29.619
The Harry Potter books and movies, give me some of that feeling.
哈利·波特的书籍和电影给了我一些这种感觉。

01:01:29.619 --> 01:01:54.119
And then sitcom wise, you know, what made me want to write sitcoms was was cheers mostly to show cheers Buffy gave me some of that And my 20s and led into the show and casting Alice and had again and it's funny I had one other thing that came up for me from her question was I just watched the Conan O'Brien mark twain prize show on Netflix, which is great Is that where everybody brings their a game and what Ferrell's so funny?
然后情景喜剧方面，你知道，让我想写情景喜剧的是欢呼声，主要是为了表达欢呼，巴菲给了我一些，我20多岁，带进了节目并选角爱丽丝，再次，有趣的是，我从她的问题中想到了另一件事，我刚刚在Netflix上观看了柯南·奥布莱恩马克·吐温奖颁奖典礼，这很棒，那是每个人都带来游戏的地方，费雷尔有什么这么有趣？

01:01:54.119 --> 01:01:58.059
I saw that clip will Ferrell so funny watch it Watch the whole thing.
我看到那个片段，费雷尔会很有趣地观看它，观看整个事情。

01:01:58.059 --> 01:02:00.260
It's all killer, no filler.
这都是杀手，没有填充物。

01:02:00.260 --> 01:02:03.980
It's like everybody comes and brings their A-game because they love Conan so much.
就好像每个人都带来了他们的顶级游戏，因为他们非常喜欢柯南。

01:02:03.980 --> 01:02:05.619
And why am I bringing that up?
我为什么要提出这个？

01:02:05.619 --> 01:02:14.099
It's because watching that made me realize how much Conan O'Brien has meant to me from 1993 premiering in Dave Letterman's old slot.
这是因为观看这部影片让我意识到，自 1993 年在戴夫·莱特曼的旧片子中首映以来，柯南·奥布莱恩对我来说意义重大。

01:02:14.099 --> 01:02:15.699
Dave Letterman, a lot to me too.
戴夫·莱特曼，对我来说也有很​​多。

01:02:15.699 --> 01:02:18.940
I wrote for Dave Letterman a few years after that.
几年后我为戴夫·莱特曼写作。

01:02:18.940 --> 01:02:20.059
I wanted to write for Conan.
我想为柯南写作。

01:02:20.059 --> 01:02:23.340
Carter and I both really were angling to write for Conan.
卡特和我都非常想为柯南写作。

01:02:23.340 --> 01:02:25.739
And they were not hiring, but Letterman was.
他们没有招聘，但莱特曼却在招聘。

01:02:25.739 --> 01:02:29.659
incredibly lucky and I love Letterman equally as much in a different way.
非常幸运，我以不同的方式同样爱莱特曼。

01:02:29.659 --> 01:02:46.260
But Conan, just watching the Netflix special about his sort of totality of his career, I felt like emotional watching it because I'm like, I just feel like I've lived 30 years with this guy and I got this brief little intersection with him where he came and spoilers, it was a background extra.
但是柯南，只要在看 Netflix 特别节目，讲述他的职业生涯的全部，我就很激动地观看它，因为我想，我只是觉得我和这个家伙一起生活了 30 年，我和他有一个短暂的小交集，他来了，剧透了，这是一个额外的背景。

01:02:46.260 --> 01:02:56.139
In an episode of How Much A Mother, we will explain that more when we get to it many years from now and after that, he knew that Carter and I were big fans And he asked us to, we asked him to lunch.
在《母亲的价值》的一集中，我们将解释更多，当我们从现在起很多年之后再讲到这一点时，他知道卡特和我是他的忠实粉丝，他邀请我们这样做，我们请他共进午餐。

01:02:56.139 --> 01:02:59.739
And so a few weeks later, we got to spend a couple hours having lunch with Conan.
几周后，我们花了几个小时与柯南共进午餐。

01:02:59.739 --> 01:03:02.619
And it was just, I just had this feeling and watching it.
只是，我只是有这种感觉并观看它。

01:03:02.619 --> 01:03:10.099
I think it's what Jessica's talking about, which is you just can't, not many things can give you the feeling that you spent your whole life with somebody.
我想这就是杰西卡所说的，那就是你不能，没有多少事情能让你感觉你和某人度过了一生。

01:03:10.099 --> 01:03:13.420
You've spent years and years and years in this world or with this energy.
你已经在这个世界上或带着这种能量度过了很多年。

01:03:13.420 --> 01:03:16.820
And so I'm so happy him, him was that to her.
所以我很高兴他，他对她来说就是这样。

01:03:16.820 --> 01:03:17.900
What is it for you, Josh?
乔什，这对你来说是什么？

01:03:17.900 --> 01:03:19.300
What comes up to you for you of that?
你对此有何感想？

01:03:19.300 --> 01:03:24.139
Like, what have I held with me this over cross, across such a long time.
就像，在这么长的时间里，我在这个十字架上带着什么。

01:03:24.139 --> 01:03:24.980
Yeah.
是的。

01:03:24.980 --> 01:03:27.940
Well, we've talked about the movie Sing Street, which is one of my favorite movies.
好吧，我们讨论了电影《歌唱街》，这是我最喜欢的电影之一。

01:03:27.940 --> 01:03:28.780
I've just seen some of it.
我刚刚看过一些。

01:03:28.780 --> 01:03:29.619
I love that movie.
我喜欢那部电影。

01:03:29.619 --> 01:03:31.960
I just re-watched that movie.
我刚刚又看了一遍那部电影。

01:03:31.960 --> 01:03:33.280
I bet Elliott likes that movie too.
我打赌埃利奥特也喜欢那部电影。

01:03:33.280 --> 01:03:34.119
Has he seen it?
他看到了吗？

01:03:34.119 --> 01:03:34.960
He hasn't seen that.
他还没有看到这一点。

01:03:34.960 --> 01:03:36.280
Yeah, that would be a great one to watch.
是的，那将是一场精彩的观看。

01:03:36.280 --> 01:03:37.400
What a music movie.
多么棒的音乐电影啊。

01:03:37.400 --> 01:03:38.840
One of the great music movies.
伟大的音乐电影之一。

01:03:38.840 --> 01:03:40.400
And great brother movies.
还有很棒的兄弟电影。

01:03:40.400 --> 01:03:43.159
Yeah, it's just works on all levels for me.
是的，它对我来说在各个层面都有效。

01:03:43.159 --> 01:03:48.519
I also, you know, I'm a huge fan of the before trilogy, the link letter.
我也是，你知道，我是前三部曲的超级粉丝，即链接信。

01:03:48.519 --> 01:03:53.199
See, that's a trilogy, because you have years and years that spans 15 years, those three movies.
看，这是三部曲，因为这三部电影年复一年地跨越了 15 年。

01:03:53.199 --> 01:03:58.559
And you get to watch them age, which is always so moving to watch people get older.
你可以看着他们变老，看着人们变老总是那么令人感动。

01:03:58.559 --> 01:04:02.599
And I just think there's something, he really catches something in those movies.
我只是觉得有些东西，他在那些电影中确实抓住了一些东西。

01:04:02.599 --> 01:04:07.599
The last one's almost like impossible to watch in some ways, because it's so tragic, but also so beautiful.
最后一个在某些方面几乎是不可能观看的，因为它是如此悲惨，但也如此美丽。

01:04:08.519 --> 01:04:10.280
But I love those.
但我喜欢那些。

01:04:11.400 --> 01:04:20.852
I'm trying to think, I mean, there's certain authors that I, just I'm always coming back to, I've talked about this before, Nick Cave does this weekly.
我试图思考，我的意思是，我总是会回想起某些作者，我之前已经讨论过这个问题，尼克·凯夫每周都会这样做。

01:04:20.852 --> 01:04:22.793
It's called the Red Hand Files.
这就是所谓的“红手档案”。

01:04:22.793 --> 01:04:25.610
And he just answers kind of like reader mail.
他只是像读者邮件一样回复。

01:04:25.610 --> 01:04:27.801
And he's the most beautiful writer.
他是最美丽的作家。

01:04:27.801 --> 01:04:28.928
He's really funny.
他真的很有趣。

01:04:28.928 --> 01:04:32.121
And it's reliably the best thing I read every week.
这确实是我每周读到的最好的东西。

01:04:32.121 --> 01:04:37.317
And I feel like I get to sit around this campfire with Nick Cave and have him tell.
我觉得我可以和尼克·凯夫一起坐在篝火旁，让他讲述。

01:04:37.317 --> 01:04:42.199
He wrote one today that was so funny about him and Nick Cage getting confused.
他今天写了一篇关于他和尼克·凯奇混淆的非常有趣的文章。

01:04:42.199 --> 01:04:50.199
And he was drinking with this guy whose wife was leaving him and he was like, my wife loves you, man.
他和一个妻子离开他的人一起喝酒，他说，我的妻子爱你，伙计。

01:04:50.199 --> 01:04:51.113
I need to tell her.
我需要告诉她。

01:04:51.113 --> 01:04:55.199
And he realized he thought he was Nick Cage, the actor, not Nick Cage, the rock star.
他意识到他以为自己是演员尼克·凯奇，而不是摇滚明星尼克·凯奇。

01:04:55.199 --> 01:05:08.199
So he ends up like writing an autograph for her and he ends up talking about, you know, like raising Arizona was a tough shoot, but the Coen brothers are so great and he was so drunk, you know, just imitating Nick Cage.
所以他最后就像给她写了一个签名，他最后谈到，你知道，就像抚养亚利桑那州是一个艰难的拍摄，但科恩兄弟太棒了，他喝醉了，你知道，只是模仿尼克·凯奇。

01:05:08.199 --> 01:05:50.800
But I love those so much and I think, I don't know, I think the campfires I tend to gravitate around are a little more probably movies or books, but you know, I grew up watching Cheers and Family Ties and, you know, that Thursday lineup, yeah, Nightcord LA Law, I mean, so I feel, I watch so much more TV when I was a kid than I do now, much to my wife, Sugar But, yeah, I mean, I don't think anyone gets in this business that we're in without having things that have really taken up residence in their psyche, you know?
但我非常喜欢这些，我想，我不知道，我认为我倾向于围绕的篝火更可能是电影或书籍，但你知道，我是看着《干杯》和《家庭纽带》长大的，你知道，周四的阵容，是的，Nightcord LA Law，我的意思是，所以我觉得，我小时候看的电视比现在多得多，对我的妻子来说，糖但是，是的，我的意思是，我不认为有人会进入这个行业我们现在还没有真正在他们的心灵中占据一席之地的东西，你知道吗？

01:05:50.800 --> 01:05:54.639
And I'm sure we'll end this and I'll think of eight more.
我相信我们会结束这个，我会想到另外八个。

01:05:54.639 --> 01:05:57.880
Well, I think you hit the nail on the head by saying the word campfire.
嗯，我认为你说的“篝火”这个词击中了要害。

01:05:57.880 --> 01:06:01.639
I think Jessica feels like she was around this campfire with us for all these years.
我想杰西卡感觉这些年来她一直和我们一起围坐在篝火旁。

01:06:01.639 --> 01:06:02.639
We're all telling stories.
我们都在讲故事。

01:06:02.639 --> 01:06:11.119
And I think it's such a gift to have that campfire kind of burn for as many, for enough years to sort of tell enough stories around.
我认为让篝火燃烧尽可能多的时间，足够长的时间来讲述足够多的故事，真是一份礼物。

01:06:11.119 --> 01:06:13.260
And I think it's so rare to get to do that.
我认为能够做到这一点是非常罕见的。

01:06:13.260 --> 01:06:15.880
That's why my brain went to like things I've spent lots of time with.
这就是为什么我的大脑开始喜欢我花了很多时间做的事情。

01:06:15.880 --> 01:06:17.559
I think that's what she's talking about.
我想这就是她所说的。

01:06:17.559 --> 01:06:19.480
So yeah, thank you, Jessica, for the question.
是的，谢谢杰西卡提出的问题。

01:06:19.480 --> 01:06:23.119
Thank you for spending that much time with us around the campfire.
感谢您与我们一起在篝火旁度过了这么多时间。

01:06:23.119 --> 01:06:24.800
And this new campfire too.
还有这个新的篝火。

01:06:24.800 --> 01:06:25.800
So thank you.
所以谢谢你。

